The file movies.csv contains information about movies released between 2020 and 2026. Each movie has a unique ID, title, year, genre, rating, runtime, and director.

Part 1: Read movie data

Complete the function read_movies(filename) to read the CSV file and create two dictionaries:
- titles: maps a movie ID (integer) to its title 
- ratings: maps a movie ID (integer) to its rating 

Use with open() to read the file, skip the first line using file.readline(), and use split(",") to separate the fields. Do not use the csv module.


Part 2: Implement two functions

Function 1: get_movie_title(movie_id, titles)

Return the title of the movie with the given ID. If the movie does not exist, return "Movie not found".

Function 2: get_highly_rated_movies(min_rating, titles, ratings)

Return a list of titles of movies with ratings greater than or equal to min_rating.

For example, calling get_highly_rated_movies(8.4, titles, ratings) should return a list containing:

["Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse", "Dune: Part Two", "The Odyssey"]

